{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py` is 793 LOC (7 under the 800 cap) and a \"god command\": it bundles the compaction **transaction** (`_compact_locked`, CCN 24), **snapshot reconstruction** (`rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log`, CCN 21), and the **CLI** surface in one file. Zero in-progress contention. Flagged by audit ae1b for both size and complexity.\n\n## Approach\nTurn `compact.py` into a thin CLI facade over two extracted engines, decomposed by responsibility (the recurrence-preventing fix — future mechanism/format changes land in the engine module, not the command file). The public CLI entry points **stay in `compact.py`** so the contended `_cli/__init__.py` dispatcher is NOT touched.\n\n1. Extract the **snapshot-reconstruction engine** → new `src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py` (~271 LOC): `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` (compact.py:437), `_build_authorship_ledger` (:74), `_snapshot_strip_keys` (:159), `_read_event_uuid` (:428), `_git_author` (:421).\n2. Extract the **compaction transaction** → new `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` (~245 LOC): `_compact_locked` (:188), `_sync_before_compact` (:63), `_maybe_pause_at_rename_barrier` (:168), `_git` (:59).\n3. `compact.py` retains the CLI facade: `compact_cli` (:598), `compact_all_cli` (:700), `_scan_snapshot_state` (:677), `_usage` (:48), `get_rebuild_count` (:43) → ~210 LOC.\n\nComplexity reduction rides on the move: pulling the authorship-ledger build and the rename barrier out of `_compact_locked` cuts its branch count, and relocating `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` into a focused module lets it be expressed as ordered phases (parse → strip → author-ledger → write). Update `.github/complexity-baseline.json` ceilings **downward only** (shrink-only ratchet).\n\nRationale (G6): the three responsibilities have different change-drivers (transaction safety, snapshot format, CLI ergonomics); separating them gives each a stable home.\n\n## Preserve public + test import paths via re-export (G1G2)\nExisting tests import RELOCATED private helpers by name from `rebar._commands.compact`:\n- `_snapshot_strip_keys` — `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:9`, `tests/unit/test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:14`.\n- `_build_authorship_ledger` — `tests/unit/test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py:362,401`.\nAnd `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` is imported by `_commands/fsck_repair.py`, `_commands/fsck.py`, and tests.\nTherefore `compact.py` must re-export ALL THREE names it moves out (`rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log`, `_snapshot_strip_keys`, `_build_authorship_ledger`) via `from .compact_rebuild import ...` (with an `__all__`/`# noqa: F401` as needed). These are plain `from ... import` consumers (not monkeypatch targets), so the re-export keeps them passing WITHOUT test edits.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact.py` — keep the CLI facade; re-export `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log`, `_snapshot_strip_keys`, `_build_authorship_ledger`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py` — NEW (snapshot reconstruction).\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` — NEW (compaction transaction).\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` — lower the ceilings for `_compact_locked` / `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` (shrink-only).\n\n## Verification (behavior-preserving refactor)\n- `compact.py` ≤ 500 LOC; complexity baseline entries equal or lower; module-size + complexity gates green.\n- Existing oracles pass unchanged: `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py`, `test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py`, `test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py`, `test_identity_4e9d_heldout.py`, `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py`, plus the compact/fsck unit tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/_commands/compact.py` ≤ 500; both new modules ≥ 100 LOC.\n- [ ] `.github/complexity-baseline.json` ceilings for `_compact_locked` and `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` are strictly ≤ their current values (24 / 21) and the shrink-only ratchet test passes.\n- [ ] `_cli/__init__.py` is unchanged (verified by `git diff --name-only` excluding it); `python -c \"import rebar._commands.compact as c; c.rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log; c.compact_cli; c.compact_all_cli; c._snapshot_strip_keys; c._build_authorship_ledger\"` resolves all five names.\n- [ ] Full default suite and all gates green with NO test edits (the four tests importing the moved private helpers pass via the re-exports)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786227771194475001,"uuid":"cb18c60c-e344-4111-8716-085774199ef5"}